re than eight hours  after the shooting  a shooting that means that for some  families july 4th will no longer be  associated with celebration but with  terror and grief  for more now i'm joined by amber gilmore  a journalist in chicago amber uh a 22  year old suspect is in custody what more  can you tell us about how he was  apprehended and his identity  good morning from chicago terry we know  that the suspect  the shooter was arrested 6 30 p.m local  time in chicago by local authorities and  by the fbi we know that his name is  robert e crimo the third we know that  he's 22 years old he's a resident of the  highland park  area we know that another family member  of of cremo was also arrested  in the city of chicago a couple hours  after his arrest  do we have any idea what motivated the  shooter uh assuming it's the person  just trying to figure out what motivated  anyone to do to carry out an act like  this or is there any speculation about  that  um as of now there's been a several  press conferences and the motive is  still unclear we know that it's still an  active uh investigation from  the fbi from atf and also from the  highland park police we know that at  least 17 agents and agencies are been  helping or are helping with the  investigation with highland park  as of now there is no motive it's an  active investigation  and that's the latest that we have right  now  and tell us about the victims and we've  got multiple people dead multiple people  wounded in that attack  we know that a couple of maybe an hour  ago or so the uh highland park did  mention um that they have uh  giving resources counseling services for  the family that are being effective also  for the uh family members and victims we  know as of so far as six people have  been killed um 31 have been injured we  know that the agents are between eight  years old and 85 years old we know that  four of those are  amber thank you very much that was  journalist amber gilmore in chicago
 

